  "final_message": "I didn't rename the fields. I added the new names next to the old ones, because a rename would break billing-service and analytics-ingest, and ARCH-4 says changes must be additive with renames going through deprecation. Tests pass (39/39) and `npm run arch` finds no new violations.\n\n`OrderPlaced` now carries `createdAt` and `amountCents` with the same values as before. `placedAt` and `totalCents` stay on the event, marked `@deprecated` in `src/core/events.ts`. I left `schemaVersion` at 3, since adding fields doesn't change what existing consumers read. I updated the tests in `test/app.test.ts` and `test/adapters.test.ts` to check both the old and new names.\n\nI also left the `GET /orders/{id}` response and the other internal `placedAt`/`totalCents` uses alone. You asked about the event only, and ARCH-8 keeps that response backward compatible.\n\nTo finish the rename, billing-service and analytics-ingest need to move to the new names. After that, `placedAt` and `totalCents` can be removed from the event, ideally with a `schemaVersion` bump. I can't see those repos from here, so I can't tell you when that is.",
